# Tutorial validation - all sections at once
# ==========================================

# --- 1. Variables & Math ---
Name is "Alice".
Age is 30.
Print "${Name} is ${Age} years old".

Total is 100 plus 50.
Tax is Total times 20 divided by 100.
Print "Total: ${Total}, Tax: ${Tax}".

Increase Total by 1.
Print "After increase: ${Total}".

# --- 2. Conditionals ---
Score is 85.
If Score is greater than or equal to 90:
    Print "Grade: A".
Otherwise if Score is greater than or equal to 80:
    Print "Grade: B".
Otherwise if Score is greater than or equal to 70:
    Print "Grade: C".
Otherwise:
    Print "Grade: F".

If Age is greater than 18 and Score is greater than 60:
    Print "Passed".

If Score is equal to 85:
    Print "Score is exactly 85".

# --- 3. Loops ---
Print "Counting 1 to 5:".
For every Number from 1 to 5:
    Print _index.

Counter is 1.
While Counter is less than 3:
    Print "While: ${Counter}".
    Increase Counter by 1.

# --- 4. Lists (Map, Filter, Sum) ---
A List Nums exists.
Nums contains 10, 20, 30, 40, and 50.

To double N:
    Result is N times 2.

Doubled is every item in Nums transformed by double.
Print "Doubled: " followed by Doubled.

Big is every item in Nums where _item is greater than 25.
Print "Big (>25): " followed by Big.

SumResult is the sum of Nums.
Print "Sum: " followed by SumResult.

# --- 5. Strings ---
Shout is (uppercase "hello").
Print "Uppercase: " followed by Shout.

Quiet is (lowercase "HELLO").
Print "Lowercase: " followed by Quiet.

Fixed is (replace "a-b-c" "-" "/").
Print "Replaced: " followed by Fixed.

# --- 6. File I/O ---
Write "hello tutorial" to the file "test_tutorial.txt".
A Text Content exists.
Read the file "test_tutorial.txt" into Content.
Print "File content: " followed by Content.
Delete the file "test_tutorial.txt".

# --- 7. Shell commands ---
A Text Listing exists.
Listing is `echo shell-works`.
Print "Shell: " followed by Listing.

# --- 8. Env vars ---
A Text Home exists.
Home is the environment variable "USERPROFILE".
Print "Home exists: " followed by "yes".

# --- 9. Try/Catch ---
Try:
    Execute the shell command `nonexistent-command-xyz`.
Catch the error into Err:
    Print "Caught error successfully".

Print "All sections passed!".
